repository-code: "https://github.com/raihan-sifat/pypi-dependency-health-study"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23007343"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23007343"
abstract: >-
  An empirical study of maintenance risk in the Python package ecosystem. The
  study analyses the top 1,000 most-downloaded PyPI packages and their
  transitive dependency trees (1,303 unique packages, 3,022 dependency
  edges) to quantify single-maintainer prevalence, rates of silent
  abandonment (>= 18 months of inactivity), and the statistical association
  between maintenance inactivity and known security advisories in the
  OSV.dev database.
